esc.body:
Sentinel found a problem that nobody handled in time, or that concerns the supervision itself.
This message BYPASSED the LLM agent, precisely because the agent may be what stopped working.

{problem}
--
machine:   {host}, uptime {uptime}
resources: disk {disk}, RAM {ram}Mi free
time:      {time}

What to check by hand:
  tail {state}/heartbeat.log
  cat  {state}/ALERT{hints}

atlas.bless_body:
{who} accepted the current snapshot as the new baseline at {when}.
Changed sections: {sections}
Baseline sha256: {sha256}
If you did not expect this, compare with `atlas.py show` and the previous baseline notice.

atlas.ack_body:
{who} acknowledged the current ALERT at {when}.
Sections: {sections}
ALERT sha256: {sha256}
Escalation for this content stops; changed content needs a new acknowledgement.

esc.ack_unrecorded:
ALERT.acked was written without `atlas.py ack` (a bare touch, or an acknowledgement of older content). Who did it is not recorded.
ALERT sha256: {sha256}
Sections: {sections}
Escalation treats the alert as acknowledged.
